input => switch current state => maybe enter new state

==============================
0 State
==============================
enter:
	[parameters]
	what to do

task:
	what to do

exit:
	what to do


==============================
1 Movement
==============================
Movement is controlled by state. Simple movement by running, jumping, e.t.c. states


==============================
1.1 Running
==============================
task:
	loop:
		//apply force or set velocity
		//lets set velocity
		P.LinearVelocity = Input.MoveDirection * speed;

		//animation control


==============================
1.2 Jump
==============================
enter:
	[direction: left/right]

task:
	//gives big impulse (in direction). P could easy stop it or make longer

	//here is example of variables
	var max = direction * maxSpeed
	var current = direction * startSpeed

	P.ApplyForce(Vector2.Up * verticalForce)
	loop:
		//force could be controlled while jump ups. Enters fall state after reaching jump peak
		//gamedesign nuances: does it starts with max speed or accelerates? Does start sets force or velocity? E.t.c
		//every loop could change velocity directly
		P.Body.LinearVelocity = ...
		//or apply forces
		P.Body.ApplyForce(...)
			
		//animation control


